\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Left: the exact symmetric revisit region \eqref  {eq:region} in the plane of bracket correlation $\rho $ and anchor value $b=d$, bounded below by the quadratic root $b_{-}$ and above by $C$. The dotted curve is the pitchfork $b=b_{\mathrm  p}$: below it the optimal interior point is the bracket middle, above it the mirror pair \eqref  {eq:offmid} hugging the ends. The dashed line is the two-shot bracket $\rho =b$, entering the region at $b^{*}=0.4233$; the upper boundary continues beyond the plotted range. Right: the value of the interior option --- the percentage increase in expected payoff of the full three-shot optimum over the best policy denied interior placements (it may still place on either exterior ray) --- as a function of the first discovered value $b$, with the bracket optimized in both cases.}}{10}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:phase}{{2}{10}{Left: the exact symmetric revisit region \eqref {eq:region} in the plane of bracket correlation $\rho $ and anchor value $b=d$, bounded below by the quadratic root $b_{-}$ and above by $C$. The dotted curve is the pitchfork $b=b_{\mathrm p}$: below it the optimal interior point is the bracket middle, above it the mirror pair \eqref {eq:offmid} hugging the ends. The dashed line is the two-shot bracket $\rho =b$, entering the region at $b^{*}=0.4233$; the upper boundary continues beyond the plotted range. Right: the value of the interior option --- the percentage increase in expected payoff of the full three-shot optimum over the best policy denied interior placements (it may still place on either exterior ray) --- as a function of the first discovered value $b$, with the bracket optimized in both cases}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {9}The three-shot policy, computed}{10}{section.9}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The three-shot game: optimal bracket correlation, log-value, the log-value with interior placement excluded (exterior rays in both directions permitted), and the percentage the interior option adds to expected payoff. Adaptive quadrature over the second value $d$; interior optima exact via the stationarity quartic \eqref  {eq:quartic}. For $b\le 0$ the optimal bracket correlation is zero and the value equals exactly $\tfrac  12+\log \!\left (1+1/\sqrt  {2\pi }\right )=0.8357\ldots  $ (Proposition~\ref {prop:below}).}}{11}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:threeshot}{{1}{11}{The three-shot game: optimal bracket correlation, log-value, the log-value with interior placement excluded (exterior rays in both directions permitted), and the percentage the interior option adds to expected payoff. Adaptive quadrature over the second value $d$; interior optima exact via the stationarity quartic \eqref {eq:quartic}. For $b\le 0$ the optimal bracket correlation is zero and the value equals exactly $\tfrac 12+\log \!\left (1+1/\sqrt {2\pi }\right )=0.8357\ldots $ (Proposition~\ref {prop:below})}{table.1}{}}
\newlabel{prop:below}{{3}{11}{Below-median start}{proposition.3}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {10}The rule as a line search}{12}{section.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:linesearch}{{10}{12}{The rule as a line search}{section.10}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The three-evaluation rule as an inner loop (\texttt  {grass3}, the heuristic adaptation of Section~10), median objective over seeds at budget 120; lower is better. The comparators are golden-section (two and six evaluations) and Brent as inner loops in a shared random-direction outer loop, and whole-cube random search. Rank is among the five; seed wins count seeds on which \texttt  {grass3} beats the best rival. Ranks average tied medians. Across all 22 objectives \texttt  {grass3} has mean rank $2.95/5$ and is first or second on eight (nine counting joint second places); \texttt  {free\_kick} is a representative loss. As a standalone optimizer the two-shot form \texttt  {grass2U} has mean rank $6.05/11$ against the eleven-method panel of Section~\ref {sec:linesearch}.}}{13}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:linesearch}{{2}{13}{The three-evaluation rule as an inner loop (\texttt {grass3}, the heuristic adaptation of Section~10), median objective over seeds at budget 120; lower is better. The comparators are golden-section (two and six evaluations) and Brent as inner loops in a shared random-direction outer loop, and whole-cube random search. Rank is among the five; seed wins count seeds on which \texttt {grass3} beats the best rival. Ranks average tied medians. Across all 22 objectives \texttt {grass3} has mean rank $2.95/5$ and is first or second on eight (nine counting joint second places); \texttt {free\_kick} is a representative loss. As a standalone optimizer the two-shot form \texttt {grass2U} has mean rank $6.05/11$ against the eleven-method panel of Section~\ref {sec:linesearch}}{table.2}{}}
